  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the probability that a randomly chosen onto function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> satisfies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> is :"
  },
