  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Total number of&nbsp;onto functions from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;tto&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></math></p><p>Now, for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnlines=\"solid none\" frame=\"solid\" rowlines=\"solid solid solid none\"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>can be defined in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#38;</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can be anything and can be defined in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Number of onto functions for which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></math></p><p>Now required probability<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
